{"step_index":302,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T16:33:46Z","input_tokens":2487,"cache_read_tokens":239798,"output_tokens":913,"content":"### Implemented: Calculations Pause on Missing or Unclear Inputs\n\nWe have updated **AUDIT IT** with a strict **Input Completeness Gatekeeper** ([`utils/auditEngine.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/auditEngine.js) & [`components/AuditScorecard.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/AuditScorecard.js)):\n\n> **Rule Enforced:** If any required detail is missing or unclear (smudged item rate, 0 quantity, missing supplier GSTIN, missing invoice number, or unreadable total), **the app halts immediately and does not calculate totals, discrepancies, or tax liabilities**. Instead, it prompts the user to provide valid inputs.\n\n---\n\n### 🛡️ How It Works\n\n#### 1. Real-Time Detection of Missing/Unclear Fields ([`utils/auditEngine.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/auditEngine.js))\nThe function `detectMissingOrUnclearInputs(invoice)` checks:\n- **Smudged / Blurry Line Items:** Rate or quantity marked as blurry, null, or $\\le 0$.\n- **Supplier GSTIN:** Missing or invalid 15-character format (unless explicitly confirmed as an unregistered vendor).\n- **Invoice Identifier:** Missing invoice or cash memo number.\n- **Declared Grand Total:** Missing or unread total on the physical parcha.\n\n#### 2. Calculations Paused Screen ([`components/AuditScorecard.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/AuditScorecard.js))\nWhen missing or unclear fields are detected:\n- **Calculations are locked:** The app sets `status: \"INPUT_REQUIRED\"`, pauses subtotal, variance checks, Section 44AD deemed profits, and CA slips.\n- **Side-by-Side Review:** The user sees their **original uploaded document on the left**, and an **\"Input Required\" interactive form on the right**:\n  - Itemized input boxes for each missing/unclear item (e.g. *\"Rate for Heavy Duty Air Bubble Wrap Roll\"*, *\"Supplier GSTIN\"*, etc.).\n  - 1-click **\"✓ Mark as Unregistered (No GSTIN)\"** button for purchases from unregistered local vendors.\n- **Action Button:** **\"🚀 Confirm Inputs & Calculate Audit\"**.\n\n#### 3. Instant Precision Calculation on Submission\nOnce the shopkeeper enters or confirms the valid values:\n- The flags are cleared and `inputs_validated` is set to `true`.\n- The deterministic calculation engine runs with full precision, displaying the item breakdown, discrepancy verdict, and unlocked Tax & ITR Insights.\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Try It Live at [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)\n\n1. **Test Missing & Blurry Bill:** Click **\"Sample 3: Missing GSTIN\"** (*Gupta Packaging Materials*).\n2. **Notice the Calculation Halt:** \n   - Totals and tax liabilities are **paused**.\n   - The app asks you to provide:\n     - Missing Supplier GSTIN (or click *\"Mark as Unregistered\"*).\n     - Smudged rate for *Heavy Duty Air Bubble Wrap Roll*.\n3. Enter the rate (e.g. `₹900`) and click **\"🚀 Confirm Inputs & Calculate Audit\"**.\n4. The calculation engine will unlock and compute the verified totals and tax breakdown instantly.","thinking":"Initial hypothesis confirmed. Calculation is paused upon detecting missing or unclear data, prompting the user for clarification before proceeding. Implemented interactive prompts, replacing premature results with requests for valid input.\n\n\n"}
{"step_index":303,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T16:40:46Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nCRITICAL PARSING RULES:\n1. HEADER VS TABLE SEPARATION:\n   - Metadata in the header or footer (Supplier Name, Address, Contact/Phone Number, GSTIN, PAN, Invoice Number, Date, Bank Details) MUST NEVER be extracted as line items.\n   - The `items` array MUST ONLY contain tangible goods, products, or billed services listed within the invoice's central itemized table.\n\n2. EXCLUSION RULES FOR ITEMS:\n   - NEVER create a line item for a GSTIN (e.g., 15-character alphanumeric strings like '06AAECM4821F1ZX').\n   - NEVER create a line item for a Phone / Mobile / Contact Number.\n   - Every valid item MUST represent a product or service with a genuine unit quantity and unit price. If a row lacks a product description or represents invoice metadata, ignore it from `items`.\n\nimport re\n\ndef clean_extracted_items(items: list) -> list:\n    cleaned = []\n    \n    # Pattern matching GSTIN (15 characters: 2 digits, 5 letters, 4 digits, 1 letter, 1 digit/letter, Z, 1 digit/letter)\n    gstin_pattern = re.compile(r'\\b\\d{2}[A-Z]{5}\\d{4}[A-Z]{1}[1-9A-Z]{1}Z[0-9A-Z]{1}\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n    # Pattern matching Indian phone numbers (10 digits, optional +91 prefix)\n    phone_pattern = re.compile(r'(\\+?91[\\-\\s]?)?[6-9]\\d{9}')\n    \n    # Common metadata keywords that should never be product names\n    forbidden_keywords = [\n        \"gstin\", \"gst no\", \"contact\", \"phone\", \"mobile\", \"tel\", \n        \"pan no\", \"bank\", \"ifsc\", \"account no\", \"invoice no\"\n    ]\n\n    for item in items:\n        desc = item.get(\"description\", \"\").strip()\n        desc_lower = desc.lower()\n\n        # 1. Skip if the description contains GSTIN patterns or phone numbers\n        if gstin_pattern.search(desc) or phone_pattern.search(desc):\n            continue\n\n        # 2. Skip if the description is just a metadata label\n        if any(keyword in desc_lower for keyword in forbidden_keywords):\n            continue\n\n        # 3. Skip invalid items with zero/negative rates or quantities\n        if item.get(\"quantity\", 0) <= 0 or item.get(\"unit_rate\", 0) <= 0:\n            continue\n\n        cleaned.append(item)\n\n    return cleaned\n\n\n\nIn the invoice processing route, apply clean_extracted_items to response.items right after the Gemini call. Ensure any item containing phone numbers, GSTIN strings, or metadata keywords is purged before passing the items to the total recalculation logic.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-02T22:10:46+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
