{"step_index":310,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T16:41:29Z","input_tokens":2892,"cache_read_tokens":247005,"output_tokens":3351,"thinking":"The code attempts to parse the Gemini response as JSON, adds metadata about the uploaded file, and then sanitizes the result. It seems that `sanitizeInvoiceData` is the likely place to address any inconsistencies in the extracted invoice items. Examining the `clean_extracted_items` or similar functions will be the next step.\n\n\nThe `clean_extracted_items` function will be applied to the Gemini response's extracted items. This function will filter items containing phone numbers, GSTIN strings, or specific metadata keywords, ensuring they are purged before total recalculation. Implementation will involve a Python script, which then can be applied to both the Python backend and the client-side JavaScript. This dual application will provide protection across both layers.\n\n\nApplying item cleaning logic to eliminate invalid invoice entries. Implemented filters for descriptions containing GSTIN, phone numbers, or metadata keywords to improve the precision of extracted item lists. Implemented checks for zero or negative quantities/rates to purge invalid entries. JavaScript equivalent of the Python script now created.\n\n\nFiltering the extracted items will eliminate entries that have patterns indicating they are metadata, such as phone numbers or GSTIN strings, or include forbidden keywords. Items containing zero or negative rates/quantities are also excluded. This strategy aims to ensure that only legitimate product entries are considered for total recalculation.\n\n\nThe item cleaning logic now explicitly excludes items with zero or negative quantities or rates, or non-positive amounts, to prevent incorrect inclusion. Also, incorporated the `cleanExtractedItems` function immediately after the Gemini response parsing to refine the extracted items. This should ensure cleaner data going forward.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"\"\"\nAUDIT IT - Item Cleaning & Exclusion Filter\nEnforces strict Header vs Table separation and purges metadata from line items.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport re\n\ndef clean_extracted_items(items: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Purges metadata, phone numbers, and GSTIN strings from extracted items array.\n    Ensures any item containing phone numbers, GSTIN strings, or metadata keywords\n    is purged before passing the items to the total recalculation logic.\n    \"\"\"\n    cleaned = []\n    \n    # Pattern matching GSTIN (15 characters: 2 digits, 5 letters, 4 digits, 1 letter, 1 digit/letter, Z, 1 digit/letter)\n    gstin_pattern = re.compile(r'\\b\\d{2}[A-Z]{5}\\d{4}[A-Z]{1}[1-9A-Z]{1}Z[0-9A-Z]{1}\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n    # Pattern matching Indian phone numbers (10 digits, optional +91 prefix)\n    phone_pattern = re.compile(r'(\\+?91[\\-\\s]?)?[6-9]\\d{9}')\n    \n    # Common metadata keywords that should never be product names\n    forbidden_keywords = [\n        \"gstin\", \"gst no\", \"contact\", \"phone\", \"mobile\", \"tel\", \n        \"pan no\", \"bank\", \"ifsc\", \"account no\", \"invoice no\",\n        \"tax invoice\", \"bill to\", \"ship to\", \"address\", \"state code\",\n        \"reverse charge\", \"e-way bill\", \"transport\", \"vehicle no\",\n        \"cash memo\", \"challan\", \"original for recipient\", \"date\"\n    ]\n\n    for item in items:\n        if not item or not isinstance(item, dict):\n            continue\n\n        desc = item.get(\"description\", \"\").strip()\n        desc_lower = desc.lower()\n\n        # 1. Skip if the description contains GSTIN patterns or phone numbers\n        if gstin_pattern.search(desc) or phone_pattern.search(desc):\n            continue\n\n        # 2. Skip if the description is just a metadata label\n        if any(keyword in desc_lower for keyword in forbidden_keywords):\n            continue\n\n        # 3. Skip invalid items with zero/negative rates or quantities\n        qty = item.get(\"quantity\") if \"quantity\" in item else item.get(\"qty\", 0)\n        rate = item.get(\"unit_rate\") if \"unit_rate\" in item else item.get(\"rate\", 0)\n        amount = item.get(\"amount\", 0)\n\n        # Ensure numeric values\n        try:\n            qty_num = float(qty) if qty is not None else 0\n            rate_num = float(rate) if rate is not None else 0\n            amt_num = float(amount) if amount is not None else 0\n        except (ValueError, TypeError):\n            continue\n\n        if (qty_num <= 0) or (rate_num <= 0 and amt_num <= 0):\n            continue\n\n        cleaned.append(item)\n\n    return cleaned\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Test cases\n    test_items = [\n        {\"description\": \"Basmati Rice 25kg\", \"qty\": 10, \"rate\": 950.0, \"amount\": 9500.0},\n        {\"description\": \"GSTIN: 07AAAAA0000A1Z5\", \"qty\": 1, \"rate\": 100.0, \"amount\": 100.0},\n        {\"description\": \"Call: +91 9876543210\", \"qty\": 1, \"rate\": 50.0, \"amount\": 50.0},\n        {\"description\": \"Bank IFSC SBIN0001234\", \"qty\": 1, \"rate\": 20.0, \"amount\": 20.0},\n        {\"description\": \"Wheat Flour Atta 50kg\", \"qty\": 5, \"rate\": 420.0, \"amount\": 2100.0},\n        {\"description\": \"Zero Qty Product\", \"qty\": 0, \"rate\": 50.0, \"amount\": 0.0}\n    ]\n    res = clean_extracted_items(test_items)\n    print(\"Cleaned Items Count:\", len(res))\n    for r in res:\n        print(\" -\", r[\"description\"])\n    assert len(res) == 2, f\"Expected 2 items, got {len(res)}\"\n    print(\"All Python test cases passed successfully!\")\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/clean_items.py"}}]}
