aded_file_url = objectUrl;\n106:           parsed.file_type = mimeType;\n107:           parsed.file_name = file.name;\n108:           return sanitizeInvoiceData(parsed);\n109:         }\n110:       }\n111:     } catch (err) {\n112:       console.warn(\"Gemini multimodal call failed; continuing with client-side OCR:\", err);\n113:     }\n114:   }\n115: \n116:   // 2. Client-side Real OCR for PDFs\n117:   if (mimeType.includes(\"pdf\") && window.pdfjsLib) {\n118:     if (onProgress) onProgress(\"Extracting text from PDF document...\");\n119:     try {\n120:       const pdfText = await extractTextFromPdf(file);"}
{"step_index":320,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T16:42:36Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. \"Build a modern web app called 'AUDIT IT' for small retail shop owners in India.   1. Create a clean, mobile-friendly dashboard with an upload dropzone where users can drop or snap a photo of an invoice (PDF or image).   2. Make the theme simple and trustworthy (slate, white, subtle emerald accents).3. Include a mock preview state showing sample invoices ready to test: one clean bill, one blurry bill, and one bill with an intentional math mistake.\"\nDo not start building or write any code yet ask me all the specifications and all features of frontend, UI,UX and core charateristics of the app on every step.   \n\n2. Create a function `generate_tax_suggestions(audit_summary, calculated_tax)` using Gemini 2.5 Flash:\n\nInput Context:\n- Total turnover and deemed profit (calculated by code)\n- Number of invoices analyzed\n- Total GST paid on purchases (potential ITC)\n- Invoices missing GSTIN (disallowed ITC)\n\nPrompt the model with:\n\"You are a tax preparation assistant for small Indian retail shopkeepers.\nGiven this pre-calculated financial data:\n{data}\n\nProvide 3 concise bullet points:\n1. Recommended ITR Form: (e.g., ITR-4 Sugam under Sec 44AD vs ITR-3) with a 1-sentence reason.\n2. GST ITC Opportunity / Risk: Explain how much Input Tax Credit can be claimed from audited bills and warn about unverified supplier GSTINs.\n3. Advance Tax & Action Item: Remind them of the March 15 advance tax deadline.\n\nTone: Grounded, simple English, no complex jargon. Include a clear disclaimer: 'Not tax advice; verify with your CA.'\"\n\nUI Dashboard AdditionIn your React frontend, add a \"Tax & ITR Insights\" tab or summary card right below the invoice audit report:Pill 1: Recommended Form: ITR-4 (Presumptive Scheme - Sec 44AD)Pill 2: Deemed Net Profit: ₹X,XX,XXX (Calculated at 6% digital / 8% cash)Pill 3: Estimated Tax Liability: ₹X,XXX (Computed via New Regime)Advisory Callout Box: Plain-English summary explaining how keeping supplier GSTINs verified maximizes their Input Tax Credit and reduces tax outgo.   \n3. great now make the app functioning with real time bills and calculations based on inputs with the suitable outputs\n4. You are an invoice parsing engine for AUDIT IT.\n\nTASK:\n1. Examine the provided document or image.\n2. First, determine if this is a genuine business invoice, cash memo, purchase bill, or tax receipt.\n3. IF IT IS NOT an invoice (e.g. it is a person's photo, landscape, screenshot of a chat, unrelated document, or random text):\n   - Set `is_valid_bill` to false.\n   - Set `rejection_reason` explaining why (e.g. \"Uploaded image is not a financial bill or invoice\").\n   - Leave all financial fields null or empty.\n4. IF IT IS AN INVOICE:\n   - Set `is_valid_bill` to true.\n   - Extract the fields as accurately as possible.\n   - NEVER make up or hallucinate missing data. If a field (like GSTIN or invoice number) is not present or unreadable, set it to null and append it to `unreadable_fields`.\n\nmake the app strictly calculate and analyse the given inputs with precision \n5. without changing the rest core features, fix the issue that original uploaded document does not match with digitized parcha shown , it currently displaying random items irrelevant to the given invoice\n6. if something seems missing or is unclear in the given document then do not move ahead and calculate just simply ask the user to give valid input \n7. CRITICAL PARSING RULES:\n1. HEADER VS TABLE SEPARATION:\n   - Metadata in the header or footer (Supplier Name, Address, Contact/Phone Number, GSTIN, PAN, Invoice Number, Date, Bank Details) MUST NEVER be extracted as line items.\n   - The `items` array MUST ONLY contain tangible goods, products, or billed services listed within the invoice's central itemized table.\n\n2. EXCLUSION RULES FOR ITEMS:\n   - NEVER create a line item for a GSTIN (e.g., 15-character alphanumeric strings like '06AAECM4821F1ZX').\n   - NEVER create a line item for a Phone / Mobile / Contact Number.\n   - Every valid item MUST represent a product or service with a genuine unit quantity and unit price. If a row lacks a product description or represents invoice metadata, ignore it from `items`.\n\nimport re\n\ndef clean_extracted_items(items: list) -> list:\n    cleaned = []\n    \n    # Pattern matching GSTIN (15 characters: 2 digits, 5 letters, 4 digits, 1 letter, 1 digit/letter, Z, 1 digit/letter)\n    gstin_pattern = re.compile(r'\\b\\d{2}[A-Z]{5}\\d{4}[A-Z]{1}[1-9A-Z]{1}Z[0-9A-Z]{1}\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n    # Pattern matching Indian phone numbers (10 digits, optional +91 prefix)\n    phone_pattern = re.compile(r'(\\+?91[\\-\\s]?)?[6-9]\\d{9}')\n    \n    # Common metadata keywords that should never be product names\n    forbidden_keywords = [\n        \"gstin\", \"gst no\", \"contact\", \"phone\", \"mobile\", \"tel\", \n        \"pan no\", \"bank\", \"ifsc\", \"account no\", \"invoice no\"\n    ]\n\n    for item in items:\n        desc = item.get(\"description\", \"\").strip()\n        desc_lower = desc.lower()\n\n        # 1. Skip if the description contains GSTIN patterns or phone numbers\n        if gstin_pattern.search(desc) or phone_pattern.search(desc):\n            continue\n\n        # 2. Skip if the description is just a metadata label\n        if any(keyword in desc_lower for keyword in forbidden_keywords):\n            continue\n\n        # 3. Skip invalid items with zero/negative rates or quantities\n        if item.get(\"quantity\", 0) <= 0 or item.get(\"unit_rate\", 0) <= 0:\n            continue\n\n        cleaned.append(item)\n\n    return cleaned\n\n\n\nIn the invoice processing route, apply clean_extracted_items to response.items right after the Gemini call. Ensure any item containing phone numbers, GSTIN strings, or metadata keywords is purged before passing the items to the total recalculation logic.\n\n<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Goal:** Build and enhance \"AUDIT IT\", a modern, trustworthy web application for Indian small retail shop owners (Kirana stores, boutiques, etc.) to audit purchase bills, verify mathematical accuracy (Qty × Rate, GST, Grand Total), check GSTIN validity, mask private details, and provide tax insights under Section 44AD presumptive taxation using Gemini 2.5 Flash.\n   - **Latest User Request:** Enforce **CRITICAL PARSING RULES** on invoice line item extraction:\n     1. *Header vs Table Separation:* Metadata in header/footer (Supplier Name, Address, Contact/Phone, GSTIN, PAN, Invoice Number, Date, Bank Details) must NEVER be extracted as line items. `items` must only contain tangible products or billed services from the central table.\n     2. *Exclusion Rules for Items:* Purge any item containing phone numbers, GSTIN strings, or metadata keywords (`gstin`, `gst no`, `contact`, `phone`, `mobile`, `tel`, `pan no`, `bank`, `ifsc`, `account no`, `invoice no`). Items with zero/negative quantities or unit rates must be skipped.\n     3. *Action:* Apply `clean_extracted_items` (or JavaScript equivalent) to `response.items` right after the Gemini call in the invoice processing route before passing items to total recalculation logic.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Workspace Directory:** `/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it`\n   - **Server:** Python HTTP server running on `http://localhost:3000` via background task `f7fe8eca-ba38-4dcb-97a7-a40aeb890237/task-65` (`server.py`).\n   - **Files Created/Updated So Far:**\n     - `utils/clean_items.py`: Created and verified with unit test (`/usr/bin/python3 utils/clean_items.py` passed). 